  "title": "Can't escape 'Code' formatting",
  "content": "<p>This forum has a new ‘<code>code</code>’ format option - for source code keywords in the middle of plain text:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/b7b96cd1-62b3-4ed5-a0dd-2bcd1e8bb3f2.png\" /></figure><p>It works fine <em>provided</em>, as above, you type the whole text first, then <em>go back</em> to add formatting.</p><p>But, if you apply the highlight at the <em>very end </em>of a <code>post, there is no way to “escape” - the whole of the rest of the post will be formatted!</code></p>",
